## Admission and ownership boundary

- `omega_state::task_admission` owns the bounded S03-001 runtime-local packet, compiler, exact-path lease registry, routing, and receipts.
- The packet closes required fields with `deny_unknown_fields`; future enum variants and omitted fields fail decoding.
- Artifact kinds include Markdown, Rust, Lean, JSON, YAML, TOML, Python, and text. A Lean kind is a typed reference only; the compiler has no Lean execution path.
- Legacy `omega.agent_work.v1` and Python lease inputs are explicit hash-bound read-only members. New writes are ten exact canonical files; patterns, globs, traversal, absolute paths, backslashes, empty segments, non-ASCII paths, case-fold collisions, whitespace/dot aliases, and Windows device names fail closed.
- Packet, observer, and source bundle hashes are independent SHA-256 receipts. Resolved evidence is opaque outside the module and can only be constructed by hashing caller-supplied bytes; every declared id, path, hash, length, and sequence member must match.
- The producer requests a write lease, but only the frozen admission host can issue it. Every active exact-path collision blocks admission.
- All packet, compilation, lease, and receipt authority effects are literally `None`.

