## Surviving obstructions

- The compiler is bounded to one frozen source closure, packet id, base commit, evidence ceiling, budget, and exact write surface. It is not a general packet-admission theorem.
- The lease registry is an in-memory deterministic verifier. It does not acquire OS locks, resolve symlinks/realpaths, write a journal, or mutate a worktree.
- Artifact bytes are supplied by the host. The production file reader and activated conductor host do not exist.
- Pattern leases remain legacy read evidence only; interoperability with active legacy journals is not claimed.
- S03-002/GTOC-7 must separately prove finite migration-bundle member preservation and terminalization after GTOC-6.
- No independent binary/process separation, human promotion, runtime gate, CI enforcement, or autonomous successor consumes the receipt.

## Nonclaims

This sprint does not execute a task, mutate a workspace, activate gates, run Lean, prove GTOC-7, certify arbitrary packet families, expose hidden artifacts, derive QM, mint authority, or make Omega Engine self-authorizing.
